super().__init__() runs A's constructor setting x = 1, then the child adds 10. The result is 11.

code:
class A:
    def __init__(self):
        self.x = 1

class B(A):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
        self.x += 10

print(B().x)  # 11

