super().__init__() with no extras runs the parent's initialization so inherited attributes get set. This is the cooperative inheritance pattern.

code:
class A:
    def __init__(self):
        self.x = 1

class B(A):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
        self.y = 2

