Every subclass constructor calls the parent constructor first so the object is fully set up.

The child forwards all keywords with super().__init__(**kw), and A uses kw.get('a', 1), so a becomes 99.

code:
class A:
    def __init__(self, **kw):
        self.a = kw.get('a', 1)

class B(A):
    def __init__(self, **kw):
        super().__init__(**kw)

print(B(a=99).a)  # 99

