Config objects pass keyword settings straight through to the base class untouched.

call(Dog()) invokes Dog.speak, which returns 'woof', because the parameter can be any object with a speak method. Result: 'woof'.

code:
class Animal:
    def speak(self): return 'generic'

class Dog(Animal):
    def speak(self): return 'woof'

def call(a):
    return a.speak()

print(call(Dog()))  # 'woof'

